```groovy
pipeline {
  agent { label 'macos && arm64' }
  options {
    timeout(time: 45, unit: 'MINUTES')
    buildDiscarder(logRotator(numToKeepStr: '30'))
  }
  environment { BUILD_TYPE = 'release' }
  stages {
    stage('Build') { steps { sh './build.sh "$BUILD_TYPE"' } }
    stage('Test')  { steps { sh 'pytest --junitxml=reports/unit.xml' } }
  }
  post {
    always  { junit 'reports/*.xml' }
    success { archiveArtifacts artifacts: 'out/*.bin', fingerprint: true }
    failure { echo 'notify owners' }
  }
}
```
- `agent` = where it runs; `stages` → `stage` → `steps` = what runs; `post` conditions: `always`, `success`, `failure`, `unstable`, `changed`, `fixed`, `regression`, `aborted`, `unsuccessful`, `cleanup`.
- `when { branch 'main' }` conditionally skips a stage. `junit` comes from the JUnit plugin.

```groovy
stage('Tests') {
  failFast true
  parallel {
    stage('Unit') { agent { label 'linux' } steps { sh 'make unit' } }
    stage('HIL')  { agent { label 'dut-pool' } steps { sh 'make hil' } }
  }
}
```
- A stage with `parallel` can't also have `steps`; each branch can have its own `agent`. Declarative doesn't allow nesting `parallel` inside a parallel branch.
- `failFast true` (or `options { parallelsAlwaysFailFast() }`) aborts sibling branches when one fails.
- `matrix { axes { axis { name 'BOARD'; values 'b1', 'b2' } } stages { ... } }` generates parallel cells for board × config combinations.
- Gotchas: branches on the same agent share one workspace (write to separate dirs); shared resources (devices, ports) need `lock`; parallelism is limited by available executors; files built on one agent must be `stash`ed/`unstash`ed to reach another.
